@startuml 08-state-order
' ShopSphere - UML state machine diagram of the Order lifecycle.
' States and rules come from requirements "Order history and tracking",
' "Stock reservation", "Order cancellation", "Return request" and
' "Order status emails" of the Requirements Specification.
skinparam defaultFontName Calibri
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 60
skinparam ranksep 60
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F4F7FC
  BorderColor #2F5496
  ArrowColor #1F3864
}

state "New" as New : entry / send "order created" email
state "Paid" as Paid : entry / send "order paid" email
state "Processing" as Processing
state "Shipped" as Shipped : entry / send email with tracking number
state "Delivered" as Delivered : entry / send "order delivered" email
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled : entry / send "order cancelled" email
state "Returned" as Returned

[*] --> New : order placed /\nreserve stock

New --> Paid : payment succeeded\n[payment method = card online] /\ncommit reservation
New --> Processing : manager confirms order\n[payment method = cash on delivery] /\ncommit reservation
Paid --> Processing : manager starts processing
Processing --> Shipped : manager ships order\n(tracking number)
Shipped --> Delivered : delivery confirmed

New --> Cancelled : payment deadline (30 min) passed\n[card online and unpaid] /\nrelease reservation
New --> Cancelled : cancelled by customer or manager /\nrelease reservation
Paid --> Cancelled : cancelled by customer or manager /\nrestock, refund
Processing --> Cancelled : cancelled by customer or manager /\nrestock, refund if paid

Delivered --> Returned : return completed\n[within 14 days after delivery] /\nrestock returned items, refund
Delivered --> [*] : [14 days after delivery\nwithout return]
Cancelled --> [*]
Returned --> [*]

note right of Processing
  Before shipment (New, Paid, Processing) a manager
  can edit items, quantities and the delivery address:
  totals are recalculated and the customer is notified;
  the status does not change.
end note

@enduml
